# Empty containers

A container (left, right, top, bottom, 2D / 3D anchor) which renders nothing is not shown. Typical cases: a `controls` widget whose parameters are always active interaction parameters presented in the toolbar (they render an empty fragment), `text` widgets without text, or an anchor opened by a selection whose parameter lives in the toolbar (it was an empty panel).

- **Decided from the data:** `isContainerEmpty(container, namespace, getDefinition)` (features/appbuilder/lib/isContainerEmpty.ts). A container is empty when it has no tabs and every widget is empty; a `text` widget is empty without `text` and `markdown`; a `controls` widget is empty when every control is a parameter reference whose parameter is unknown, hidden (`overrides.hidden` applies), or an interaction parameter (`selection`, `gumball`, `rectangleTransform`, `drawing`) whose presentation resolves to toolbar (`resolveInteractionPresentation`, always active by default; the drawing keeps `activeMode` / `presentation` in `settings.props.general`, `overrides.settings` are applied). An `accordion` widget is empty without exports when every parameter renders nothing and no group header would render (hidden and unknown parameters are skipped; a group with more than one visible parameter renders its header, the theme default `avoidSingleComponentGroups` suppresses the header of a single one). Every other widget or control counts as content. Nothing is measured or observed in the DOM. Selection, gumball and rectangle transform are `Interaction` parameters told apart by `settings.type` with their settings in `settings.props`; the drawing is a parameter type of its own (`Drawing`) with `settings.general` at the top level.
- **The node is still rendered.** The components inside an empty container keep working: an always active interaction parameter presented in the toolbar creates its gizmo and its toolbar entry from inside the container, so the container must never be unmounted to hide it. `useAppBuilderStandardContainers` sets `empty` on the template container (`IAppBuilderTemplatePageContainer.empty`); the templates (`AppBuilderAppShellTemplatePage`, `AppBuilderGridTemplatePage`) lay an empty container out like an absent one (collapsed navbar / header, `display: none` sections, grid areas without it) while rendering its node. On desktop the AppShell navbar content is always live (`navbarContentLive`): it is only collapsed while empty, and an idle (`Activity` hidden) subtree would run no effects. `useViewportAnchors` passes `empty` to the anchors; `AnchorContainer` hides the panel (`display: none`, `data-app-builder-anchor={id}`, `data-app-builder-anchor-empty`) while its content is rendered as usual, the open / close state is untouched.
- Both hooks depend on the parameter stores (`useShapeDiverStoreParameters.parameterStores`) and on the App Builder data, so a container appears once its text widgets receive text with a later output or its parameters are (re)defined. Content which appears without new data or definitions (e.g. a progress widget while a computation runs) is not detected: such a container counts as content.
- Tests: `containerElement(page, "left")` is not in the viewport for an empty left container (the collapsed navbar is moved off-screen, `toBeHidden` does not apply), `anchorPanel(page, id)` exists and is hidden for an empty anchor.
- Details: the accordion check counts group headers by group name (the accordion default `identifyGroupsById: false`); `dragging` is empty only with an explicit `presentation: "toolbar"` (it defaults to the widget presentation in every active mode). Empty AppShell slots (`top`, `left`, a `bottom` or `right` moved into the navbar) render their wrapper with `hidden` (`display: none`) so they take no space beside other content; the navbar idles each container separately on mobile and never idles an empty one (it only holds components working outside of it, e.g. toolbar-presented interaction parameters, which would otherwise never register while the drawer is closed or hidden). Below the mobile breakpoint an empty anchor injects its content into the standard container inside a hidden box marked with `data-app-builder-empty-content` (`EMPTY_CONTENT_ATTRIBUTE`); Content moved by `mobileFallback` from an empty source container is injected the same way (`useAppBuilderStandardContainers`). `isWidgetEmpty` treats such a marked element as empty, any other injected element as content.
- Do not solve an empty container by changing what a widget renders (e.g. switching an interaction parameter to the widget presentation inside anchors): the rule is global and the container simply is not shown.
